# Settings for `docker compose`. Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in.

# The PostgreSQL database the app uses. Plain postgresql:// URLs, as hosting
# providers give them, work as they are.
# Railway: from your own machine, use the database's public URL
# (DATABASE_PUBLIC_URL). The private one (host postgres.railway.internal)
# only resolves for services deployed in the same Railway project.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE

# Signs sign-in sessions. Optional locally; anywhere real, use a long random
# value (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`).
# JWT_SECRET=

# E-mail. Without these, e-mails are only written to the backend's log.
# Example for Gmail (needs 2-Step Verification on the Google account; the
# password is an *App Password*, not your normal one: Google Account >
# Security > 2-Step Verification > App passwords. Paste it without spaces):
# EMAIL_BACKEND=smtp
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USERNAME=you@gmail.com
# SMTP_PASSWORD=your-16-letter-app-password
# SMTP_FROM=you@gmail.com
# Then check it with:
#   docker compose exec backend python -m app.send_test_email --to you@gmail.com

# Booking assistant (customers' chat). One Groq key (console.groq.com) runs both the
# model and the guards; without it the chat says it isn't set up yet.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# The model that talks: openai/gpt-oss-120b (default) or openai/gpt-oss-20b (lighter, more mistakes).
# CHAT_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# low (default), medium or high: more reasoning is more accurate but uses more tokens.
# CHAT_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# The guard that answers ALLOW or BLOCK for every message and reply.
# GUARD_TOPIC_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
# Prompt Guard, a cheap first filter for jailbreak wording; leave empty to switch it off.
# GUARD_INJECTION_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-prompt-guard-2-86m
# GUARD_INJECTION_THRESHOLD=0.8
# Contacting the admin from the chat: the reply time customers are promised, and how often each can ask.
# CHAT_HELP_RESPONSE_HOURS=6
# CHAT_HELP_REQUESTS_PER_WEEK=3
# Self-hosted with Ollama instead (nothing leaves your servers; GROQ_API_KEY can be any text):
# GROQ_BASE_URL=http://ollama:11434/v1
# CHAT_MODEL=gpt-oss:20b
# GUARD_TOPIC_MODEL=gpt-oss:20b
# GUARD_INJECTION_MODEL=
